{
  "title": "NMOS current mirror (SKY130)",
  "group": "Electronics — analog",
  "description": "SKY130 NFET current mirror: diode-connected MN1 sets the reference current, MN2 mirrors it; sweep the output voltage to see the flat current-source characteristic, stepped reference current via RREF",
  "schematic": {
    "notes": [
      {
        "x": 40,
        "y": -190,
        "title": "SKY130 NMOS current mirror — what this testbench does",
        "lines": [
          "Real SKY130 nfet_01v8 (1.8 V core) devices, BSIM4.8 via OSDI.",
          "Diode-connected MN1 (gate tied to drain) sinks the reference",
          "current set by RREF from VDD = 1.8 V, so IREF ~ (VDD - VGS)/RREF.",
          "MN1 and MN2 share the same gate and grounded source, so MN2",
          "copies MN1's VGS and mirrors that current. Each bulk (b) is tied",
          "to ground.",
          "",
          "VOUT sweeps MN2's drain 0 -> 1.8 V. iout is flat once MN2",
          "saturates (VOUT > Vov) -- that flat level is the mirrored",
          "current, and its slight upward slope is the finite output",
          "resistance (DIBL / channel-length modulation from the real",
          "model). 1-ohm sense resistors turn each branch current into a",
          "probe voltage (iout ~ V/1ohm).",
          "",
          "MN1 and MN2 are the same size (2 um / 1 um), so this is a 1:1",
          "mirror -- iout copies IREF. RREF.R is stepped 8k / 4k / 2k, which",
          "raises IREF from ~78 uA to ~160 uA, and each iout curve tracks it",
          "flatly (the copy is within a few percent of IREF).",
          "",
          "SKY130 device widths are baked into the extracted model card and",
          "can't be swept, so to change the mirror ratio set MN2.w_um (e.g.",
          "4.0 for ~2:1) and re-run -- recompiles once per new width, then",
          "cached."
        ]
      }
    ],
